		(uuid "0c8d1095-c189-4234-aae3-fc841c75ffa8")
	)
	(text "Function: U7 translates TMS from FTDI3.3V to XEM1.8V.\nSource / changes: Opal Kelly BRK8305 A03,25Oct2023,\nJTAG sheet8/PDFp4: U504/C525/C526 -> U7/C40/C41.\nhttps://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/583/download?category_id=3\nSame SN74AXC1T45DBVR and two100nF values; topology unchanged.\nCodex redraw follows BRK row spacing and vertical bypass layout.\nRail names: USBJTAG_3.3V / XEM_1.8V; DGND renamed GND.\nTI SCES882E,Dec2023,pp3,18:\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/sn74axc1t45.pdf\nDIR5=3.3V (A-to-B). PCB/powered operation remain unverified."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 433.705 530.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3cc6698f-4e33-4a9c-9c8d-5445cc4730aa")
	)
	(text "Function: U5 translates TDI from FTDI3.3V to XEM1.8V.\nSource / changes: Opal Kelly BRK8305 A03,25Oct2023,\nJTAG sheet8/PDFp4: U502/C515/C516 -> U5/C36/C37.\nhttps://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/583/download?category_id=3\nSame SN74AXC1T45DBVR and two100nF values; topology unchanged.\nCodex redraw follows BRK row spacing and vertical bypass layout.\nRail names: USBJTAG_3.3V / XEM_1.8V; DGND renamed GND.\nTI SCES882E,Dec2023,pp3,18:\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/sn74axc1t45.pdf\nDIR5=3.3V (A-to-B). PCB/powered operation remain unverified."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 433.705 464.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "41b15a73-a4be-4879-8c7b-e4358c7026cb")
	)
	(text "Function: U1 converts 12 V to the main carrier 3.3 V rail. R3/R4/C10 form its feedback network.\nTP2 probes 3.3 V after L1; TP3 probes 1.5 V. D3/R14 indicate voltage presence (about 0.5 mA\nnominal), not power-good status.\nU2 derives 1.5 V from 3.3 V when enabled by XEM_PG.\n\nSource / changes: Inherited TI-style TPS54429E circuit; V6 placement/routing is a Codex\nadaptation for RSA16. TI SLVSAS0 (February 2011), p. 5 RSA pin map, p. 14 Table 1 and p. 16\nFigure 16. Figure 16 shows PWP14; it is guidance, not an unchanged RSA layout.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps54429e.pdf\nR3 = 73.2 kohm, R4 = 22.1 kohm and C10 = 10 pF match the TI 3.3 V row. Inherited L1 = 3.3 uH\ndiffers from that row's 2.2 uH. C3/C4 = 22 uF/100 nF, C8/C9 = 2 x 22 uF, R2 = 10 kohm VIN-to-EN\nare retained. No electrical value/netlist changes in V6.\nThermal-via implementation is documented in the V6 routing handoff. Effective capacitance,\nload/startup/stability, thermal behavior and assembly remain unqualified.\nTest/indicator branches were designed by Codex. D3: Kingbright AA1608LCGSK, DSAQ3027 V2B, 1\nMarch 2025, pp. 1-3 (package/polarity/pads, electrical data and curves).\nhttps://www.kingbrightusa.com/images/catalog/SPEC/AA1608LCGSK.pdf\nR14: Vishay D/CRCW e3, document 20035 (0603, 1%, 0.1 W).\nhttps://www.vishay.com/docs/20035/dcrcwe3.pdf\nTP arrangement: TI SLVU444A, Rev. A, August 2021, p. 6, Table 4-1. LED pads follow the\nmanufacturer; courtyard/silk are Codex choices. Brightness at 0.5 mA and probe access remain\nunverified.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ug/slvu444a/slvu444a.pdf\nU2: TI TLV755P, SBVS320D, September 2024, p. 3 DQN pins, p. 15 section 7.1.1, p. 21 Figure 7-6.\nInherited C11/C12 = 4.7 uF and R5 = 100 kohm XEM_PG pulldown are retained; effective\ncapacitance and loading remain unverified.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tlv755p.pdf\nThermal-via reference: RSA0016B drawing 4219093/A, August 2021, datasheet PDF pp. 23-24; TI QFN\nand SON PCB Attachment, SLUA271C, December 2023, section 3.4.1 p. 7. Opposite-face tenting and\nthe retained nine-window stencil require assembly/voiding review.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/an/slua271b/slua271b.pdf"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 328.295 295.91 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "53f605c8-128c-48ef-96eb-2ab852b703d3")
	)
	(text "VBuck_3.3V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 293.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5750fe9a-5c09-4b75-af23-872d17f22789")
	)
	(text "Function: J4 is a horizontal USB2 device socket; cable entry is parallel to the PCB.\nR6/R7 are CC pulldowns; C16/FB2 connect shield to GND at high frequency.\nSource / changes: GCT USB4110-GF-A, USB4110 revB4,22May2024,sheet1/2:\nhttps://gct.co/files/drawings/usb4110.pdf\nCodex adapts BRK8305 A03,25Oct2023,JTAG sheet8/PDFp4:\nJ500/R500/R501/FB503/C522 -> J4/R6/R7/FB2/C16.\nhttps://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/583/download?category_id=3\nPCB alternative replaces USB4105 with USB4110 and four SMT shell stakes.\nBaseline saved schematic still named vertical USB4120; this proposal fixes J4\nmetadata.\nAll20 pin identities, UUIDs and wiring retained;16 A/B contacts unchanged.\nKiCad10 USB4110 footprint copied;4 SH pads renamed M1-M4.\nX/Y front face unchanged; mating height1.68mm vs USB4105 1.73mm (0.05mm Z).\n3D is an inherited datasheet-derived shell envelope, not manufacturer CAD.\nR6/R7=5.1k,FB2=220ohm at100MHz,C16=100nF; BRK DNP straps omitted.\nD+/D- duplicated contacts joined; SBU unused. USB_D_P/N to U3.7/.6.\nUSB5V is separate from carrier12V/buck3.3V. No USB data/VBUS ESD array.\nEnclosure/cable fit, ESD/EMI and assembly remain unverified."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 35.56 538.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "635543e1-b989-4b54-beb0-425cc6041f2d")
	)
	(text "Function: U6 translates TDO from XEM1.8V to FTDI3.3V.\nSource / changes: Opal Kelly BRK8305 A03,25Oct2023,\nJTAG sheet8/PDFp4: U503/C519/C520 -> U6/C38/C39.\nhttps://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/583/download?category_id=3\nSame SN74AXC1T45DBVR and two100nF values; topology unchanged.\nCodex redraw follows BRK row spacing and vertical bypass layout.\nRail names: USBJTAG_3.3V / XEM_1.8V; DGND renamed GND.\nTI SCES882E,Dec2023,pp3,18:\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/sn74axc1t45.pdf\nDIR5=GND (B-to-A). PCB/powered operation remain unverified."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 433.705 497.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "696ced93-e56f-4a22-a7c0-0fc7d657f8de")
	)
	(text "Level shifters (BRK8305 style)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 338.455 416.56 0)
		(effects
